__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
data/raw/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
springboot-app/target/
.DS_Store
# The agent's own settings, which are a property of this machine rather
# than of this project: they set a permission mode and an allowlist, and
# a copy of them in a public repository is a copy that runs on whoever
# clones it. The skills are the exception: they say how this project is
# checked, shipped and audited, and the agents in CI (claude.yml, the
# review, the audits, the autofix) read them from the checkout.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# The editor's per-machine state. The only file ever committed here was
# an empty setting VS Code's Python extension wrote on its own.
.vscode/

.env

# Trained model artifacts. Regenerable from the labels and code
# (collect -> engineer-features -> retrain -> promote, all seeded on
# RANDOM_STATE), and versions/ gains another copy on every promote, so
# these accumulate rather than settle.
data/models/
# The pilot's own ratings, made on this machine in the app (the chart
# picks) or before it (the older spottability ratings, emptied for fresh
# ones on 2026-10-01): hand judgment, kept on the machine and its iCloud
# copy, not in the repository -- committed, every rating made showed as a
# change, and the repository's copy was the old ratings the pilot had
# cleared. The checkpoint notes stay committed. And what the pipeline
# builds from a corridor's candidates: its features, and the map of them
# the data-collection notebook draws.
data/labels/chart_picks.csv
data/labels/spottability_ratings.csv
data/processed/features_*.parquet
data/processed/candidates_map.html
# The chart model's training table (vfr.chartmodel), which the planner
# writes from the ratings when a retrain starts.
data/processed/chart_training.parquet


# The local HTTPS certificates infra/local-https/make-certs.sh writes: a
# private key and a CA for one machine, never for the repository.
infra/local-https/certs/

# iCloud writes a numbered copy beside a file it thinks two machines
# both changed ("main 2.tsx"). One of those was committed on
# 2026-09-22 by a `git add -A`: a stale duplicate of main.tsx that
# nothing imported and that had missed a change. They are never
# wanted here.
* [0-9].*

# vfr.routecsv's lock files and the temporary files it renames into place.
data/labels/*.lock
data/labels/.*.tmp

# The TV apps built by tv/package.sh.
tv/out/
